cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "safemodetree: from an FMEA table to a checked fault-response policy, with safe-mode reachability and ambiguity-class analysis"
abstract: >-
  Takes an FMEA-shaped declaration - faults with an effect, an ordinal severity
  category, a detectability flag and a declared detection latency; modes
  including declared safe modes; responses with a transition, a cost and a
  precondition; and an observability model of which faults are distinguishable
  from which observations - builds the response automaton and checks that a
  declared safe mode is reachable from every fault state under the declared
  detection assumption. Reports unreachable safe modes, fault states with no
  response, responses whose preconditions can never hold, and ambiguity classes
  where two faults are indistinguishable but demand different responses. A
  calibrated multinomial-logistic fault classifier is benchmarked against the
  declared threshold-logic baseline at an equal false-alarm rate, and the
  policy consumes its confidence: a low-confidence identification is routed to
  the conservative response for the whole ambiguity class, and the cost of that
  conservatism is measured in declared outage minutes. The threshold baseline
  is not beaten on identification accuracy and that result is reported.
  Research-grade; not flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for
  operational aerospace use.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-15"
license: Apache-2.0
